    "## Important findings before final submission", "",
    "### 1. The prediction time still needs correction", "",
    "The README now recognises that the source dataset is based on historical values relative to the day before arrival. That is a useful correction to the original brief. However, changing the description to 'risk for upcoming bookings using details up to the day before arrival' does not make the current evaluation a prospective one-day-ahead cancellation forecast.", "",
    f"Among the 44,198 retained cancelled bookings, {a['prediction_landmark_check']['status_before_day_before_arrival']:,} ({100*a['prediction_landmark_check']['status_before_day_before_arrival']/44198:.2f}%) have a cancellation status date strictly before the day before arrival. {a['prediction_landmark_check']['status_on_or_before_day_before_arrival']:,} ({pct(a['prediction_landmark_check']['already_known_fraction'])}) have it on or before that day. These bookings were generally no longer active bookings awaiting cancellation at that proposed landmark. Date-only records do not establish within-day ordering.", "",
    "A proper landmark evaluation would select bookings still active at the prediction time and predict cancellations after it, using inputs captured at that time. The current score classifies historical cancelled/non-cancelled records. It does not establish performance for that prospective task, nor for booking confirmation. Removing reservation_status and reservation_status_date prevents direct outcome input but does not reconstruct earlier predictor snapshots.", "",
    "For the report's original confirmation-time application, verify or reconstruct the predictors as they stood then. Deposit type is derived from payments before arrival/cancellation, and ADR from lodging transactions, so their CSV values are not automatically confirmation-time inputs. Parking and special requests can be added or amended later. Waiting-list days describe time before confirmation and are not automatically outcome leakage. Even ordinary booking descriptors may change later.", "",
    "### 2. The strict comparison changes more than duplicate retention", "",
