    "The retained scenarios group identical predictor profiles; the strict scenario does not. The 73% versus 81% comparison therefore changes the split safeguard, row weights and class prevalence. It is not a controlled demonstration that retaining repetitions trains a better model. The accompanying new experiment fixes group membership across both policies and evaluates both winners on the same populations.", "",
    "### 3. Rare-category encoding can merge different raw inputs", "",
