    "The README appropriately discloses that the simplified inputs were developed after the grouped test result was seen and that an initial grouping bug was fixed. Preserve that disclosure. The current test is held out within the corrected run but is not independent evidence untouched throughout project development. Do not repeatedly modify the system until this known test crosses 80%.", "",
    "### 7. Keep the improved explanations", "",
    "The README correctly treats genuine separate repeated bookings as an assumption, not a proven fact, and SHAP as associations rather than causes. These are improvements over the earlier brief. I inspected the supplied global and local SHAP figures: they are consistent with XGBoost explanations in log-odds, and the global importance file identifies deposit type and country as leading associations. I did not rerun SHAP. Dropping arrival year alone does not demonstrate future or Malaysian performance.", "",
    "## Practical recommendation", "",
    "Keep the simplified form and the raw-input grouping implementation as useful foundations. Use 79.73% as the current verified simplified historical test F1. Complete the missing artifacts and environment pins. Resolve the prediction-time claim before calling this the final system described by the proposal. Choose a duplicate policy based on the unit of analysis and present the alternative as sensitivity evidence, rather than choosing it solely to cross 80%.", "",
    "The audit found credible reproducible results for the supplied simplified model, not grounds to call the work fabricated. It also did not establish that the complete experiment or dashboard meets every proposal requirement.", "",
    "## Evidence and reproduction", "",
